# (HELMS wave 2) end caps

# (HELMS forge-fix i2) begin (forge fix 2, the owner: "winged helms look alike at 1x; make the variants bolder"): `when
# helmfam-winged,<mass>` replace views, one bold outline per body-mass class (the first replacing view that holds wins).
# the broad mass keeps the base blades; the eagle: a cast eagle on the crown, its wings spread
# flat to a wide bar; the fin: one tall swept pinion on the crown; the messenger: small wings swept back on a pointed helm.
# Written by the HELMS area tools/d2.py (D R drawn; U is D with the face details dropped; L is R mirrored and re-lit).
# the eagle (none, mantle)
# (FORGE-HEAD envelope r2, tools2/brass.py) A1-A3: on a dark sheen (the antique brasses) this outline takes a metal shading: a narrow lit band and specular streak, the mid-step body, a shadowed quarter, a glint on the brim's lip
